<title>USA: IADB launches 9.6 bln yen Eurobond issue.</title>
<headline>IADB launches 9.6 bln yen Eurobond issue.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Inter-American Development Bank (IADB) on Tuesday launched a 9.6 billion yen medium-term bond issue, with maturity scheduled for 2007.</p>
<p>The 3.07 percent annual coupon will be paid in U.S. dollars and the issue was priced at 100.20 percent, the IADB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The issue, arranged by IBJ International Plc, will add to the ordinary capital of the IADB for investments in the social and economic development of Latin America and the Caribbean, the statement said.</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsdesk 202-898-8300))</p>
